   "subject": "1D GP analytical inference with direct sum kernel",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">Hi all,</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">To all the GP experts, would really appreciate if you can\r\nshed some light to this direct kernel sum problem.</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">Let X and Y be a set of 1-D predictor and observation respectively</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">y(x_i) = n(x_i) + s(x_i) + err_i</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">where  n(x) is\r\nGP with a neural network kernel, s(x) is a GP with a SE kernel and e_i ~ N(0,\r\nsigma). </font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">Following R&amp;W, </font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">k(x, x’) = k_n(x, x’) + k_s(x, x’)</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">where k, k_n, k_s are the kernel for y, n and s respectively and I is the identity matrix</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">Let A = [k_n(X, X) + k_s(X, X) + sigma^2 * I]^(-1)</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">I can implement the analytical solution for y in STAN with:</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">mu(y) = (k_n(X_tilde, X) + k_s(X_tilde, X)) * A * y</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">cov(y) = (k_n(X_tilde, X_tilde) + k_s(X_tilde, X_tilde)) –\r\n(k_n(X_tilde, X) + k_s(X_tilde, X)) * A * t((k_n(X_tilde, X) + k_s(X_tilde, X))\r\n+ sigma^2*I</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">And the estimate for y looks reasonable.</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">Now, I want to find the analytical solution for n(X_tilde)\r\nand s(X_tilde) assuming n(x) and s(x) to be independent.</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">From above, the means seem to be clear:</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">mu(n) = k_n(X_tilde, X) * A * y</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">mu(s) = k_s(X_tilde, X) * A * y</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">But, how about cov(n) and cov(s)?</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">Let N_tilde = k_n(X_tilde, X) and S_tilde = k_s(X_tilde, X)</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">cov(y) </font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">= (k_n(X_tilde, X_tilde) + k_s(X_tilde, X_tilde)) – (N_tilde\r\n+ S_tilde) * A * t((N_tilde + S_tilde)) + sigma^2*I</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">= k_n(X_tilde, X_tilde) – N_tilde * A * t(N_tilde) + </font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">   k_s(X_tilde,\r\nX_tilde) – S_tilde * A * t(S_tilde) + </font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">   sigma^2\r\n* I + </font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">   N_tilde\r\n* A * t(S_tilde) + S_tilde * A * t(N_tilde)</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">Following the logic of this (<a href=\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1507.00566.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://arxiv.org/pdf/1507.00566.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792461031787000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1b5tA3aWVaUqVg_iNYzS6v\">https://arxiv.org/pdf/1507.00566.pdf</a>),\r\nit seems to me that:</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">cov(n) = k_n(X_tilde, X_tilde) – N_tilde * A * t(N_tilde)</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">cov(s) = k_s(X_tilde, X_tilde) – S_tilde * A * t(S_tilde)</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">If this is true, the following needs to\r\nhold?</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">N_tilde * A * t(s_tilde) + S_tilde * A * t(N_tilde) = 0</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">such that cov(y) = cov(n) + cov(s) + sigma^2 * I</font><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">My questions are:</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">1.<span style=\"line-height:normal\">     </span>1. am I missing something with my maths?</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">2.<span style=\"line-height:normal\">    \r\n</span>2. if not, how can I supply a prior to enforce this\r\nconstrain in STAN?</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">Many thanks,</font><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">Andy</font><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "IC2mXK4yCAAJ",
   "from": "Aki Vehtari",
   "author": "a236d3d356ca53fd",
   "date": "2016-06-27T17:00:31Z",
   "subject": "Re: 1D GP analytical inference with direct sum kernel",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">It seems you want something similar as in R&amp;W Section 5.4.3 Manua Loa example where there are four covariance functions (eq 5.19), and Figure 5.7 shows different components (or the birthday example in BDA3). <div>You can think of your model as </div><div> y = f + e</div><div>where you can have</div><div>1) f=n+s, e=err</div><div> or if you want to focus on one of the components</div><div>2a) f=n, e=s+err<br>2b) f=s, e=n+err</div><div>Then you can use the usual equations (which you know already) to compute mu(f) and cov(f) for these different choices.</div><div>In a way when making predictions you choose which part is the interesting signal (f) and which part is the nuisance parameter (e).</div><div><br></div><div>Aki</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>On Monday, June 27, 2016 at 12:00:04 PM UTC+3, <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">andy...@cubist-asia.com</a> wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">Hi all,</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">To all the GP experts, would really appreciate if you can\r\nshed some light to this direct kernel sum problem.</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">Let X and Y be a set of 1-D predictor and observation respectively</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">y(x_i) = n(x_i) + s(x_i) + err_i</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">where  n(x) is\r\nGP with a neural network kernel, s(x) is a GP with a SE kernel and e_i ~ N(0,\r\nsigma). </font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">Following R&amp;W, </font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">k(x, x’) = k_n(x, x’) + k_s(x, x’)</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">where k, k_n, k_s are the kernel for y, n and s respectively and I is the identity matrix</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">Let A = [k_n(X, X) + k_s(X, X) + sigma^2 * I]^(-1)</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">I can implement the analytical solution for y in STAN with:</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">mu(y) = (k_n(X_tilde, X) + k_s(X_tilde, X)) * A * y</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">cov(y) = (k_n(X_tilde, X_tilde) + k_s(X_tilde, X_tilde)) –\r\n(k_n(X_tilde, X) + k_s(X_tilde, X)) * A * t((k_n(X_tilde, X) + k_s(X_tilde, X))\r\n+ sigma^2*I</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">And the estimate for y looks reasonable.</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">Now, I want to find the analytical solution for n(X_tilde)\r\nand s(X_tilde) assuming n(x) and s(x) to be independent.</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">From above, the means seem to be clear:</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">mu(n) = k_n(X_tilde, X) * A * y</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">mu(s) = k_s(X_tilde, X) * A * y</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">But, how about cov(n) and cov(s)?</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">Let N_tilde = k_n(X_tilde, X) and S_tilde = k_s(X_tilde, X)</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">cov(y) </font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">= (k_n(X_tilde, X_tilde) + k_s(X_tilde, X_tilde)) – (N_tilde\r\n+ S_tilde) * A * t((N_tilde + S_tilde)) + sigma^2*I</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">= k_n(X_tilde, X_tilde) – N_tilde * A * t(N_tilde) + </font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">   k_s(X_tilde,\r\nX_tilde) – S_tilde * A * t(S_tilde) + </font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">   sigma^2\r\n* I + </font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">   N_tilde\r\n* A * t(S_tilde) + S_tilde * A * t(N_tilde)</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">Following the logic of this (<a href=\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1507.00566.pdf\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://arxiv.org/pdf/1507.00566.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792461031789000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0NBLikQDotUXUy6GbSdt1h\">https://arxiv.org/pdf/1507.00566.pdf</a>),\r\nit seems to me that:</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">cov(n) = k_n(X_tilde, X_tilde) – N_tilde * A * t(N_tilde)</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">cov(s) = k_s(X_tilde, X_tilde) – S_tilde * A * t(S_tilde)</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">If this is true, the following needs to\r\nhold?</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">N_tilde * A * t(s_tilde) + S_tilde * A * t(N_tilde) = 0</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">such that cov(y) = cov(n) + cov(s) + sigma^2 * I</font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">My questions are:</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">1.<span style=\"line-height:normal\">     </span>1. am I missing something with my maths?</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">2.<span style=\"line-height:normal\">    \r\n</span>2. if not, how can I supply a prior to enforce this\r\nconstrain in STAN?</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">Many thanks,</font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">Andy</font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> </font></p>\r\n\r\n</blockquote></div></div>"
